### Test User Views API - Dev Environment
### 
### IMPORTANT: SECRETS CONFIGURATION
### ===================================
### This file uses environment variables from http-client.env.json for secrets.
### The http-client.env.json file is already in .gitignore and will not be committed.
### 
### To set up your environment:
### 1. Create http-client.env.json in this directory (if it doesn't exist)
### 2. Add your secrets to the "dev" environment section:
### 
### {
###   "dev": {
###     "baseUrl": "https://your-api-gateway-url.execute-api.region.amazonaws.com/",
###     "authToken": "your-jwt-token-here",
###     "cognitoClientId": "your-cognito-client-id",
###     "cognitoRegion": "your-cognito-region",
###     "userPoolId": "your-user-pool-id",
###     "cognitoDomain": "your-cognito-domain",
###     "testUsername": "your-test-username",
###     "testPassword": "your-test-password"
###   }
### }
### 
### HOW TO GET SECRETS:
### ===================
### 1. Base URL: Run `terraform output api_gateway_url` in dev workspace
### 2. Cognito User Pool ID: From AWS Cognito console or terraform outputs
### 3. Cognito Client ID: From AWS Cognito console or terraform outputs  
### 4. Cognito Region: The AWS region where your resources are deployed
### 5. Cognito Domain: From AWS Cognito console (App integration > Domain name)
### 6. Test User: Create a test user in Cognito with USER role
### 7. Auth Token: Get JWT token by authenticating with Cognito (see request below)
### 
### Base URL for dev environment can be found with:
###      terraform workspace select dev
###      terraform output api_gateway_url
###
### Prerequisites:
### 1. You must have a valid Cognito user with USER role
### 2. Set up http-client.env.json with your secrets
### 3. The token must include "cognito:username" claim

### ============================================
### AUTHENTICATION - Get JWT Token
### ============================================

### 0. Get JWT Token from Cognito
# This will return an IdToken that you should copy and use as {{accessToken}}
# Uses testUsername and testPassword from http-client.env.json
POST https://cognito-idp.{{cognitoRegion}}.amazonaws.com/
Content-Type: application/x-amz-json-1.1
X-Amz-Target: AWSCognitoIdentityProviderService.InitiateAuth

{
  "AuthFlow": "USER_PASSWORD_AUTH",
  "ClientId": "{{cognitoClientId}}",
  "AuthParameters": {
    "USERNAME": "{{testUsername}}",
    "PASSWORD": "{{testPassword}}"
  }
}

