### ============================================
### PUBLIC ENDPOINTS (No authentication required)
### ============================================

### 1. GET Random Quote (unauthenticated - no view recording)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote

### 2. POST Quote with exclusions (unauthenticated)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote
Content-Type: application/json

[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

### 3. Get All Liked Quotes (public endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/liked
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ============================================
### USER VIEWS ENDPOINTS (NEW - Require authentication)
### ============================================

### 4. GET Random Quote (authenticated - will record view)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. GET View History (requires authentication) - NEW ENDPOINT https://sy5vvqbh93.execute-api.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/api/v1/quote/viewed
# Returns all quotes viewed by the authenticated user in chronological order
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/viewed
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7. GET history (deprecated: is not used in the frontend)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/history
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ============================================
### LIKE/UNLIKE ENDPOINTS (Require authentication)
### ============================================

### 8. Like a Quote (requires authentication)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/79/like
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 9. Unlike a Quote (requires authentication)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/quote/79/unlike
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 11. Get view history (should be empty for new user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/viewed
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12. Try to get view history without authentication (should return 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/viewed

### 13. Try to like without authentication (should return 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quote/1/like
Content-Type: application/json

### 14. Try to unlike without authentication (should return 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/quote/1/unlike

### 15. Get liked quotes (should be in order 1, 2, 3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/quote/liked
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 16. Reorder quote 3 to position 1 (moving up)
# Play to see what it does:
# - gives the quote with given id the position of the contents
# - the original quote and following quotes are moved 1 up. The quotes with lower order number stay in their original place.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/quote/3/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order": 2
}

### 17. Try to reorder with invalid order (0 or negative - should return 400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/quote/1/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order": 0
}

### 18. Try to reorder with invalid order (negative - should return 400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/quote/79/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order": -1
}

### 19. Try to reorder a quote that user hasn't liked (should be ignored)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/quote/61/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order": 1
}

### ============================================
### NOTES
### ============================================
#
# User Views Feature:
# - GET /quote with authentication automatically records the view
# - GET /quote without authentication does NOT record views (uses local storage on frontend)
# - GET /quote/history returns all quotes viewed by authenticated user (chronological order)
# - GET /quote/history requires authentication (returns 403 without token)
# - Viewed quotes are automatically excluded when fetching new quotes (authenticated users)
# - Views are stored in separate DynamoDB table: quote-lambda-tf-user-views-dev
#
# Expected Behavior:
# - Each authenticated user has their own view history
# - Unauthenticated users don't have server-side view tracking
# - View history is ordered by viewedAt timestamp (oldest first)
# - Authenticated users won't see the same quote twice (excluded automatically)
# - View recording happens automatically on every /quote request with auth
#
# Reorder Favourites Feature (NEW):
# - PUT /quote/{id}/reorder: Reorder a liked quote to a new position
# - Requires authentication with USER role
# - Request body: { "order": <positive integer> }
# - Automatically updates all affected likes to maintain sequential ordering
# - Moving up: increments quotes between new and old position
# - Moving down: decrements quotes between old and new position
# - Returns 204 No Content on success
# - Returns 400 if order is not a positive integer
# - Returns 403 if user doesn't have USER role
# - Silently ignores if quote is not in user's likes
#
# Like Ordering:
# - New likes automatically get order = maxOrder + 1 (added to end)
# - Liked quotes are returned sorted by order (ascending)
# - Order values are always sequential (1, 2, 3, ...) with no gaps
#
# DynamoDB Tables:
# - quote-lambda-tf-user-views-dev: Stores user views (username, quoteId, viewedAt)
# - quote-lambda-tf-user-likes-dev: Stores user likes (username, quoteId, likedAt, order)
# - quote-lambda-tf-quotes-dev: Stores all quotes
#
